ck, and it gets smaller. That gives option 2. Option 4 is tempting because it is folded and turned correctly, but it is still wavy and not smaller.", "trick": "When a figure changes in many ways, list every change (fold, turn, shading, size) and remove options that miss even one. Shading and size are the fastest to check.", "confidence": "high", "note": "PDF answer B (grey button confirmed by pixel brightness) fits the figures."}